# Cubion Jungle — stylized arcade art direction

Colorful stylized low-poly / Fall Guys candy party-game look. Quality comes from silhouette + materials + lighting + color + depth — not poly count or photo textures.

## Hard constraints

- Preserve gameplay geometry, origins, object names, and collisions.
- Never delete gameplay / obstacle / Col_* / Obs_* objects without explicit approval.
- Put new decorative objects in dedicated collections (`GRAPHICS_UPGRADE`, `FOLIAGE_KIT`).
- Prefer modular assets and linked/instanced copies over unique one-offs.
- Prefer large clean shapes; avoid small noisy detail.
- Keep the center of the gameplay board readable.
- Use rounded bevels and soft shading.
- Avoid photorealistic textures and high-frequency noise.
- Avoid excessive bloom, metallic look, and black crushed shadows.
- Preserve the current gameplay / review camera unless asked otherwise.
- Before large Blender operations: save a `_backup` copy under `art/jungle/backups/`.
- After every stage: validate scene, then viewport screenshot or preview render; wait for user approval before the next stage.
- Favor Eevee-compatible materials and game-ready geometry.
- Ask before applying destructive modifiers.
- Never change object names used by game code / export filters.

## Art direction checklist

- Stylized low-poly, rounded toy forms
- Saturated but not neon-acid colors
- Large readable props; modular foliage kit (3–7 objects per cluster)
- Flat / light procedural materials (Principled BSDF), no photo albedos
- Soft warm Sun + cool fill; AO; soft shadows
- Toy cyan water: depth tint, large soft ripples, foam planes, no mirror ocean
- Three depth planes: foreground framing, mid board+character, cool distant foliage
- Island edge: thick cliff silhouette + hanging vines, not a thin floating slab

## Work cycle (mandatory)

1. Diagnose only (no edits)
2. One category per turn (board → mats → light → water → foliage → edge → character → depth → post)
3. Validate + preview
4. User review
5. Next stage

## Runtime sync

After Blender backdrop/prop export, update `public/assets/maps/jungle/**` and keep `src/game/themes/jungle.js` Fall Guys candy palette (no photo maps except soft water scroll).
